ered in the Yenisey River basin in 1838-39, starting the Siberian gold rush. Up to 1876 the Yenisey basin had the largest goldfields in the empire, producing more than 20 percent of Russia\'s gold. After that year, the Lena River goldfields predominated, by 1908 employing some thirty thousand people.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1963, 'temperature': 0.2})
